Yep, I've actually done this, as part of my unending campaign to abuse
the executable until something breaks.  It always does.  That's why it's
called netHACK!  ;-)

The secret is that your pet doesn't become untame so long as you aren't
gone from its level too long; so, let a half dozen tame rats surround
you at stair head, descend, wait a turn or two to let them disperse so
they don't go back up with you, ascend, wait for more to gather,
descend, etc.

I'm not sure that thirty would be possible without lots of patience, but
I've gotten over a dozen to go with me this way pretty easily.

